sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant S as service (as sentinel_app, not superuser)
  participant PG as Postgres
  S->>PG: BEGIN
  S->>PG: SELECT set_config('app.tenant_id', 'acme', true)
  S->>PG: SELECT … FROM knowledge_chunks WHERE tenant_id = 'acme'
  PG->>PG: policy: tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')
  PG-->>S: only acme rows
  S->>PG: COMMIT (setting ends with the transaction)
  Note over S,PG: No tenant bound → setting is NULL → policy matches nothing (fail closed)
  Note over S,PG: Superusers bypass RLS even with FORCE → services never use one
